  "text": "Assistant: Let's detail the solution step by step:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Identify the Centers and Radii of the Circles\n#### Circle \\( C_1 \\):\nThe equation is \\( x^2 + y^2 - 2x - 4y + 1 = 0 \\). To find the center and radius, complete the square:\n\\[\nx^2 - 2x + y^2 - 4y = -1\n\\]\n\\[\n(x^2 - 2x + 1) + (y^2 - 4y + 4) = -1 + 1 + 4\n\\]\n\\[\n(x-1)^2 + (y-2)^2 = 4\n\\]\nThus, the center of \\( C_1 \\) is \\( (1, 2) \\), and its radius is \\( 2 \\).\n\n#### Circle \\( C_2 \\):\nThe equation is \\( x^2 + y^2 + 2x - 6y + 2 = 0 \\). To find the center and radius, complete the square:\n\\[\nx^2 + 2x + y^2 - 6y = -2\n\\]\n\\[\n(x^2 + 2x + 1) + (y^2 - 6y + 9) = -2 + 1 + 9\n\\]\n\\[\n(x+1)^2 + (y-3)^2 = 8\n\\]\nThus, the center of \\( C_2 \\) is \\( (-1, 3) \\), and its radius is \\( 2\\sqrt{2} \\).\n\n---\n\n### 2. Find the Distance Between the Centers\nThe distance \\( d \\) between the centers \\( (1, 2) \\) and \\( (-1, 3) \\) is:\n\\[\nd = \\sqrt{(1 - (-1))^2 + (2 - 3)^2} = \\sqrt{4 + 1} = \\sqrt{5}\n\\]\n\n---\n\n### 3. Find the Equation of the Perpendicular Line\nThe line segment \\( P_1P_2 \\) is perpendicular to the line passing through the centers. The slope of the line passing through the centers is:\n\\[\nm = \\frac{3 - 2}{-1 - 1} = \\frac{1}{-2} = -\\frac{1}{2}\n\\]\nThus, the slope of the perpendicular line is the negative reciprocal, which is \\( 2 \\). Using the point-slope form, the equation of the perpendicular line is:\n\\[\ny - 2 = 2(x - 1)\n\\]\n\\[\ny = 2x\n\\]\n\n---\n\n### 4. Find the Points of Tangency \\( P_1 \\) and \\( P_2 \\)\nThe tangent lines to \\( C_1 \\) and \\( C_2 \\) must be at least distance \\( d = \\sqrt{5} \\) away from the centers.\n\n#### Tangent to \\( C_1 \\):\nThe tangent line to \\( C_1 \\) at \\( P_1 \\) will have the form:\n\\[\ny - 2 = m(x - 1)\n\\]\nWe need to ensure this line is at a distance of \\( \\sqrt{5} \\) from \\( (1, 2) \\). The distance \\( \\text{dist} \\) is:\n\\[\n\\text{dist} = \\sqrt{\\frac{m^2 + 1